  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 247 AM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\n(Thursday - Friday)\n\nDry weather with near to below normal temperatures are still \nexpected to end the work week as a weak surface anticyclone moves \ninto the mid-Mississippi Valley.\n\n\n(Friday Night - Tuesday)\n\nThere remains some subtle, but notable, differences with the large \nscale pattern across the CONUS this weekend into early next week. \nThe EPS remains deeper and farther to the west with the midlevel \ntrough across the Great Lakes. This sends a cooler air mass far \nenough west into our region, and keeps us largely dry. The GEFS is \nweaker with the trough and a bit to the east. That means our area \nbarely gets brushed with the cooler air mass, and sets up a \npotential MCS Sunday night into Monday morning as the \"ring of fire\" \nsets up more to the east and more into the mid-Mississippi Valley \ncompared to the central Plains.",
